2026-11-27 19:42:19.947 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I\'ve gathered enough to report. Note: all tool calls are now being refused ("not allowed during a background review"), so this report is based on what I collected before that point.\n\n## Report: css-tree repo — lexer, shorthand, fork(), test harness\n\n### 1. Project shape\n- Repo is **css-tree v3.2.1** (JavaScript/ESM, `"type": "module"`), **not a Python project**. There is **no `pytest` harness and no `*.py` files anywhere** in the repo.\n- Source lives in `lib/`, tests in `lib/__tests/`, build output in `cjs/` and `dist/`.\n\n### 2. CSS lexer implementation (exact paths)\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` | The `Lexer` class — the whole public lexer API (511 lines) |\n| `lib/lexer/index.js` | Barrel: `export { Lexer } from \'./Lexer.js\';` |\n| `lib/lexer/match.js` | `matchAsTree(tokens, matchGraph, lexer)` — core matcher |\n| `lib/lexer/match-graph.js` | `buildMatchGraph(syntax, ref)` — compiles definition-syntax AST → match graph |\n| `lib/lexer/prepare-tokens.js` | `prepareTokens(value, syntax)` — value → token list |\n| `lib/lexer/generic.js`, `generic-const.js`, `generic-an-plus-b.js`, `generic-urange.js` | Generic type definitions (`<length>`, `an+b`, `urange`, …) |\n| `lib/lexer/structure.js` | `getStructureFromConfig(config)` |\n| `lib/lexer/search.js` | `matchFragments(...)` |\n| `lib/lexer/trace.js` | trace helpers spread into match results |\n| `lib/lexer/error.js` | `SyntaxReferenceError`, `SyntaxMatchError` |\n| `lib/lexer/units.js` | unit groups |\n| `lib/syntax/create.js` | `createSyntax(config)` — wires `lexer`, `createLexer`, `fork()` |\n| `lib/syntax/config/mix.js` | config merge used by `fork()` |\n\n### 3. Existing lexer API / signatures (`lib/lexer/Lexer.js`)\n```js\nexport class Lexer {\n  constructor(config, syntax, structure)          // config: {generic, cssWideKeywords, units, types, atrules, properties, node}\n\n  checkStructure(ast)                             // → false | [{node, message}]\n  createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent = null)\n  addAtrule_(name, syntax)\n  addProperty_(name, syntax)\n  addType_(name, syntax)\n\n  checkAtruleName(atruleName)\n  checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName)\n  checkPropertyName(propertyName)\n\n  matchAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  matchAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, descriptorName, value)\n  matchDeclaration(node)\n  matchProperty(propertyName, value)\n  matchType(typeName, value)\n  match(syntax, value)                            // syntax: string | descriptor\n\n  findValueFragments(propertyName, value, type, name)\n  findDeclarationValueFragments(declaration, type, name)\n  findAllFragments(ast, type, name)\n\n  getAtrule(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtrulePrelude(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, name)\n  getProperty(propertyName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getType(name)\n\n  validate()                                      // → null | {errors, types, properties}\n  dump(syntaxAsAst, pretty)\n  toString()\n}\n```\nInternal helpers in the same file: `dumpMapSyntax`, `dumpAtruleMapSyntax`, `valueHasVar(tokens)`, `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier(syntax)`, `buildMatchResult(matched, error, iterations)`, `matchSyntax(lexer, syntax, value, useCssWideKeywords)`.\n\nMatch result shape: `{ matched, iterations, error, ...trace }` (trace from `lib/lexer/trace.js`).\n\nDescriptor shape (`createDescriptor`): `{ type, name, parent, serializable, syntax, match, matchRef }`, with lazy getters for `syntax` (parsed on first access) and `match` (graph built on first access); `matchRef` exists only for `type === \'Property\'` and is non-null only when the syntax is a single top-level comma multiplier.\n\n### 4. Shorthand handling\n- **There is no shorthand support today.** A content search for `shorthand` across `lib/**/*.js` returned **zero matches**; across `*.md` only two unrelated CHANGELOG hits ("Expanded the lexer\'s dump output…", "Expand definitions using the `fork()` method").\n- No `expand`/`compress`/`shorthand` module exists in `lib/lexer/`. Shorthand expansion would be a new capability, most naturally added as a new method on `Lexer` (e.g. `expandShorthand`/`compressShorthand`) plus a helper module under `lib/lexer/`, exported through `lib/lexer/index.js` if needed.\n- Related existing machinery you\'d build on: `matchProperty` → `matchSyntax` → `matchAsTree` (gives you the matched token tree), `prepareTokens`, and `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier` (already the pattern for "this property is a comma list").\n\n### 5. `fork()` custom-syntax support\n`lib/syntax/create.js`:\n```js\nfork(extension) {\n    const base = mix({}, config);            // copy of config\n    return createSyntax(\n        typeof extension === \'function\'\n            ? extension(base)                // function form: mutate/return config\n            : mix(base, extension)           // object form: merged over base\n    );\n}\n```\n- `createSyntax(config)` builds `{ lexer, createLexer, tokenize, parse, generate, walk, find, findLast, findAll, fromPlainObject, toPlainObject, fork }` and instantiates `new Lexer({generic, cssWideKeywords, units, types, atrules, properties, node}, syntax)`.\n- `createLexer: config => new Lexer(config, syntax, syntax.lexer.structure)`.\n- Config merge semantics: `lib/syntax/config/mix.js`; a leading `|` in a syntax string appends to the existing definition (see tests below).\n- Public entry: `lib/index.js` re-exports `fork` (and `lexer`, `createLexer`) from the syntax module.\n\n### 6. Test harness — **mocha, not pytest**\n- `package.json` scripts:\n  - `npm test` → `mocha lib/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter progress`\n  - `npm run test:cjs` → `mocha cjs/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter progress`\n  - `npm run test:dist` → `mocha dist/__tests --reporter progress`\n  - `npm run lint` → `eslint lib scripts && node scripts/review-syntax-patch --lint && node scripts/update-docs --lint`\n  - `npm run coverage` → `c8 --exclude lib/__tests --reporter=lcovonly npm test`\n- **The command to run is `npm test`** (or `npx mocha lib/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js`). `python -m pytest -q` will collect nothing — there are no Python files.\n- Test helper: `lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js` (module resolution for `css-tree`), plus `lib/__tests/helpers/index.js`, `JsonLocator.js`, `common.js`.\n\n### 7. Where shorthand tests should be added\n- **Primary: `lib/__tests/lexer.js`** — the lexer unit-test file (171 lines). It already imports `{ lexer, createLexer, fork } from \'css-tree\'` and contains the `fork()`-based "should allow append definitions" `describe` block (properties/types append via `| foo`), plus `validate()`, units, and CSS-wide-keyword tests. New `describe(\'shorthand\', …)` blocks belong here.\n- **Secondary (fork/custom-syntax behavior):** `lib/__tests/common.js` — contains the `it(\'fork()\', …)` test and a `describe(\'selector\', …)` block using `fork(syntaxConfig => …)`.\n- **Fixture-based (if shorthand needs parse/generate round-trips):** `lib/__tests/fixtures/` (e.g. `fixtures/stringify.css` referenced from `common.js`), driven by `lib/__tests/parse.js` / `lib/__tests/generate.js`.\n- Other lexer-adjacent test files that may need touching if the API surface changes: `lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js`, `lexer-match-type.js`, `lexer-match.js`, `lexer-match-result.js`, `lexer-check-property-name.js`, `lexer-search-fragments.js`, `lib/__tests/exports.js` (asserts the public export list — add any new export there).\n\n### 8. Caveats\n- `patch.json` exists at repo root (found by filename search) but I could not read its contents — reads were blocked before I got to it. It is likely a syntax-data patch file consumed by `scripts/review-syntax-patch`; worth checking before adding property definitions.\n- `lib/__tests/lexer.js` lines 121–171 were not read (blocked); the tail of the file is unverified.\n- No `pytest`/Python harness exists; if the task\'s acceptance criteria assume `python -m pytest -q`, that assumption does not match this repository and should be confirmed with the parent agent.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2252, 'prompt_tokens': 33142, 'total_tokens': 35394, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 32896}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 32896, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 246}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': 'e439a63e-8fda-4389-b2e9-949ec6af150b', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21cd0-1c4f-7ff0-b8c7-7b8e30c59b53-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 33142, 'output_tokens': 2252, 'total_tokens': 35394, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 32896}, 'output_token_details': {}}
