2026-11-27 19:42:34.822 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough to report. Note: tool access was cut off mid-inspection (sandbox refused `terminal`, then read/search tools were blocked), so a few items are marked as unverified.\n\n## Report: css-tree repo — lexer / shorthand / fork / test harness\n\n### 1. Project identity & layout\n- Repo is **css-tree v3.2.1** (JavaScript, ESM, `"type": "module"`), **not a Python project**.\n- Root: `package.json`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `patch.json`, `csstree.cjs`, `csstree.esm.js`, `data/`, `lib/`, `scripts/`, `cjs/`, `dist/`.\n- Source of truth is `lib/` (ESM). `cjs/` and `dist/` are **build artifacts** generated by `npm run build` (`scripts/esm-to-cjs.cjs`, `scripts/bundle`) — do not hand-edit.\n\n### 2. CSS lexer implementation (exact paths)\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` | The `Lexer` class (511 lines) — all public API |\n| `lib/lexer/index.js` | `export { Lexer } from \'./Lexer.js\';` |\n| `lib/lexer/match.js` | `matchAsTree(tokens, matchGraph, lexer)` — core matcher |\n| `lib/lexer/match-graph.js` | `buildMatchGraph(syntax, ref)` — syntax AST → match graph |\n| `lib/lexer/prepare-tokens.js` | `prepareTokens(value, syntax)` — value → token array |\n| `lib/lexer/generic.js`, `generic-const.js`, `generic-an-plus-b.js`, `generic-urange.js` | generic type definitions (`<length>`, `an-plus-b`, `urange`, …) |\n| `lib/lexer/units.js` | unit groups (`length`, `angle`, …) |\n| `lib/lexer/structure.js` | `getStructureFromConfig(config)` |\n| `lib/lexer/search.js` | `matchFragments(...)` |\n| `lib/lexer/trace.js` | trace helpers spread into match results |\n| `lib/lexer/error.js` | `SyntaxReferenceError`, `SyntaxMatchError` |\n| `lib/syntax/create.js` | `createSyntax(config)` — wires `Lexer` into the syntax object, defines `fork()` |\n| `lib/syntax/config/mix.js` | config merge used by `fork()` |\n| `lib/data.js`, `lib/data-patch.js` | default syntax data (mdn-data + patch) |\n\n### 3. Existing lexer API / signatures (`lib/lexer/Lexer.js`)\n```js\nexport class Lexer {\n  constructor(config, syntax, structure)      // config: {generic, cssWideKeywords, units, types, atrules, properties, node}\n\n  // descriptors\n  createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent = null)   // type: \'Property\' | \'Type\' | \'AtrulePrelude\' | \'AtruleDescriptor\'\n  addAtrule_(name, syntax)\n  addProperty_(name, syntax)\n  addType_(name, syntax)\n\n  // checks (return Error | undefined)\n  checkAtruleName(atruleName)\n  checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName)\n  checkPropertyName(propertyName)\n  checkStructure(ast)                          // → warnings[] | false\n\n  // matching (return {matched, iterations, error, ...trace})\n  matchAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  matchAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, descriptorName, value)\n  matchDeclaration(node)\n  matchProperty(propertyName, value)\n  matchType(typeName, value)\n  match(syntax, value)                         // syntax: string | descriptor\n\n  // fragments\n  findValueFragments(propertyName, value, type, name)\n  findDeclarationValueFragments(declaration, type, name)\n  findAllFragments(ast, type, name)\n\n  // lookups\n  getAtrule(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtrulePrelude(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, name)\n  getProperty(propertyName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getType(name)\n\n  validate()                                   // → {errors, types, properties} | null\n  dump(syntaxAsAst, pretty)                    // → {generic, cssWideKeywords, units, types, properties, atrules}\n  toString()\n}\n```\nModule-level helpers in the same file: `dumpMapSyntax`, `dumpAtruleMapSyntax`, `valueHasVar(tokens)`, `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier(syntax)`, `buildMatchResult(matched, error, iterations)`, `matchSyntax(lexer, syntax, value, useCssWideKeywords)`.\n\nDescriptor shape (created by `createDescriptor`): `{ type, name, parent, serializable, syntax, match, matchRef }`, with lazy getters for `syntax` (parsed on first access) and `match` (graph built on first access); `matchRef` exists only for `type === \'Property\'` and is non-null only when the syntax is a top-level comma multiplier.\n\n### 4. Existing shorthand handling\n**There is none.** A content search for `shorthand|expand|compress` across `lib/**/*.js` returned **0 matches**, and `lib/lexer/` contains no shorthand/expansion module. The lexer only validates/matches values against definition syntax; it has no notion of shorthand ↔ longhand expansion or compression. Any shorthand feature must be added new (natural home: a new `lib/lexer/shorthand.js` or methods on `Lexer`, plus config plumbing in `lib/syntax/create.js`).\n\n### 5. `fork()` custom-syntax support\n`lib/syntax/create.js`:\n```js\nfork(extension) {\n    const base = mix({}, config);            // copy of config\n    return createSyntax(\n        typeof extension === \'function\'\n            ? extension(base)                // function form: receives base config, returns new config\n            : mix(base, extension)           // object form: merged over base\n    );\n}\n```\n- Exported from `lib/index.js` (alongside `lexer`, `createLexer`, `parse`, `generate`, `walk`, `find`, `findAll`, `fromPlainObject`, `toPlainObject`, `version`, `tokenTypes`).\n- Config keys consumed by `Lexer`: `generic`, `cssWideKeywords`, `units`, `types`, `atrules`, `properties`, `node`.\n- `mix()` (`lib/syntax/config/mix.js`) supports the `\'| …\'` append convention (e.g. `properties: { color: \'| foo\' }` appends to the existing definition) — see `lib/__tests/lexer.js:98-122`.\n- `fork()` is also used for round-tripping via `lexer.dump()` (`lib/__tests/lexer.js:161-169`), so **any new config key must be added to `dump()`** or recovery tests will silently drop it.\n\n### 6. Test harness — important correction\n- **There is no pytest harness and no Python code in this repo.** `search_files` for `*.py` / `test_*.py` / `pytest` / `conftest` returned zero results.\n- The harness is **mocha** (devDependency `mocha ^9.2.2`), driven by npm scripts in `package.json`:\n  - `npm test` → `mocha lib/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter progress`\n  - `npm run test:cjs` → same over `cjs/__tests`\n  - `npm run test:dist` → `mocha dist/__tests`\n  - `npm run lint` → `eslint lib scripts && node scripts/review-syntax-patch --lint && node scripts/update-docs --lint`\n  - `npm run build-and-test` → build + `test:dist` + `test:cjs`\n- `lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js` installs a `__proto_pollute__` guard on `Object.prototype` that throws on non-own property reads — new code must use `Object.create(null)` / `hasOwnProperty` style access.\n- `python -m pytest -q` (the command in my working rules) **will not work here**; the equivalent verification command is `npm test` (optionally `npx mocha lib/__tests/lexer*.js --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js` for a focused run).\n\n### 7. Where shorthand tests should be added\nAll under `lib/__tests/` (mirror into `cjs/__tests` only via the build, never by hand):\n| File | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/__tests/lexer.js` | Lexer construction, `createLexer`, `fork()` config plumbing, `validate()`, `dump()`/recovery — add shorthand-config and dump-round-trip tests here |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js` | `Lexer#matchProperty()` behavior (vendor prefixes, hacks, css-wide keywords) — add shorthand expansion/compression assertions here |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-match.js` | generic `Lexer#match()` |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-match-type.js` | `Lexer#matchType()` |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-match-result.js` | match-result shape (`matched`, `error`, `iterations`) |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-check-property-name.js` | property-name checks |\n| `lib/__tests/lexer-search-fragments.js` | fragment search |\n| `lib/__tests/helpers/index.js` | shared helpers (`lazyValues`, `cssWideKeywords`) used by the lexer tests |\n| `lib/__tests/fixture/definition-syntax.js` | `forEachTest` fixture driver used by `lexer-match-property.js` |\n\nIf shorthand gets its own module, the conventional addition is a new `lib/__tests/lexer-shorthand.js` following the `describe(\'Lexer#…\')` + `assert` style of the existing files.\n\n### 8. Caveats / unverified\n- `terminal` was refused (`SANDBOX_POLICY=auto`, no OS sandbox backend for subagent scope), so I could not run `npm test`, `ls`, or `git status`; all findings come from file reads and content searches.\n- `patch.json` exists at repo root but `read_file` resolved it to `/patch.json` and failed — its contents are unverified.\n- `lib/__tests/helpers/index.js` and the tail of `lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js` (lines 81-151) were not read before tool access was revoked; the helper exports (`lazyValues`, `cssWideKeywords`) are inferred from the import at `lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js:3`.\n- `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` line 511 is the last line; the file ends with `toString()`.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2511, 'prompt_tokens': 36073, 'total_tokens': 38584, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 35840}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 35840, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 233}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': '8bc11ec9-cda6-4d1a-9df3-44b1a1afaf95', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None} id='lc_run--01a21cd0-5202-7e10-a0b3-29f8673a10e8-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 36073, 'output_tokens': 2511, 'total_tokens': 38584, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 35840}, 'output_token_details': {}}
