2026-11-27 19:42:45.683 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough to report. Note: tool execution (terminal/python) is blocked in this subagent context (`SANDBOX_POLICY=auto`, no sandbox backend), so the report is based on static inspection only.\n\n## Report: css-tree repo — lexer, shorthand, fork(), test harness\n\n### 1. Project shape\n- Repo root is **css-tree v3.2.1** (ESM, `"type": "module"`), source in `lib/`, tests in `lib/__tests/`.\n- **There is no Python code and no pytest harness.** No `*.py`, no `conftest.py`, no `pytest.ini`/`pyproject.toml` anywhere in the tree. The test runner is **mocha** (`devDependencies.mocha ^9.2.2`).\n\n### 2. CSS lexer implementation (exact paths)\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` | The `Lexer` class (511 lines) — all matching/validation logic |\n| `lib/lexer/index.js` | `export { Lexer } from \'./Lexer.js\';` |\n| `lib/lexer/match.js` | `matchAsTree(tokens, matchGraph, lexer)` — core matcher |\n| `lib/lexer/match-graph.js` | `buildMatchGraph(syntax, ref)` — compiles definition syntax → match graph |\n| `lib/lexer/prepare-tokens.js` | `prepareTokens(value, syntax)` — value → token list |\n| `lib/lexer/generic.js`, `generic-const.js`, `generic-an-plus-b.js`, `generic-urange.js` | generic type definitions |\n| `lib/lexer/structure.js` | `getStructureFromConfig(config)` |\n| `lib/lexer/search.js` | `matchFragments(...)` |\n| `lib/lexer/trace.js`, `error.js`, `units.js` | trace helpers, `SyntaxReferenceError`/`SyntaxMatchError`, unit tables |\n| `lib/syntax/create.js` | `createSyntax(config)` — wires `lexer`, `createLexer`, `fork()` |\n| `lib/syntax/config/mix.js` | config merge used by `fork()` |\n| `lib/index.js` | public exports (`lexer`, `createLexer`, `fork`, `parse`, `generate`, `walk`, …) |\n\n### 3. Existing lexer API / signatures (`lib/lexer/Lexer.js`)\n```js\nexport class Lexer {\n  constructor(config, syntax, structure)          // config: {generic, cssWideKeywords, units, types, atrules, properties, node}\n\n  checkStructure(ast)                             // -> false | [{node, message}]\n  createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent = null)\n  addAtrule_(name, syntax)\n  addProperty_(name, syntax)\n  addType_(name, syntax)\n\n  checkAtruleName(atruleName)\n  checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName)\n  checkPropertyName(propertyName)\n\n  matchAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)\n  matchAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, descriptorName, value)\n  matchDeclaration(node)\n  matchProperty(propertyName, value)\n  matchType(typeName, value)\n  match(syntax, value)\n\n  findValueFragments(propertyName, value, type, name)\n  findDeclarationValueFragments(declaration, type, name)\n  findAllFragments(ast, type, name)\n\n  getAtrule(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtrulePrelude(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, name)\n  getProperty(propertyName, fallbackBasename = true)\n  getType(name)\n\n  validate()                                      // -> null | {errors, types, properties}\n  dump(syntaxAsAst, pretty)\n  toString()\n}\n```\nModule-level helpers (not exported): `dumpMapSyntax`, `dumpAtruleMapSyntax`, `valueHasVar(tokens)`, `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier(syntax)`, `buildMatchResult(matched, error, iterations)`, `matchSyntax(lexer, syntax, value, useCssWideKeywords)`.\n\nMatch result shape: `{ matched, iterations, error, ...trace }` (trace = `isType`/`isProperty`/`isKeyword`/`getTrace`).\n\nDescriptor shape: `{ type, name, parent, serializable, syntax, match, matchRef }`; `syntax` and `match` are lazily defined via `Object.defineProperty` getters; `matchRef` exists only for `type === \'Property\'`.\n\n### 4. Shorthand handling — **none exists**\n- Grep for `shorthand|expand|compress` across `lib/**/*.js` and `*.md`: **zero matches**.\n- There is no shorthand expansion/compression module, no `expandShorthand`/`compressShorthand` API, no shorthand entries in the syntax config. Any shorthand feature is green-field.\n- The closest existing machinery to build on:\n  - `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier()` + `descriptor.matchRef` (single-term match graph for comma-separated lists) — `lib/lexer/Lexer.js:55-64`, `:217-235`.\n  - `matchAsTree` / `buildMatchGraph` for per-component matching.\n  - `lib/lexer/prepare-tokens.js` for tokenizing a value.\n\n### 5. `fork()` custom-syntax support\n`lib/syntax/create.js:31-39`:\n```js\nfork(extension) {\n    const base = mix({}, config);            // copy of config\n    return createSyntax(\n        typeof extension === \'function\'\n            ? extension(base)                // function form: receives base config, returns new config\n            : mix(base, extension)           // object form: merged over base\n    );\n}\n```\n- `mix` lives in `lib/syntax/config/mix.js`; string values starting with `|` **append** to an existing definition (see `lib/__tests/lexer.js:98-122`).\n- `createSyntax` also exposes `createLexer(config)` → `new Lexer(config, syntax, syntax.lexer.structure)`.\n- `fork()` is exported from `lib/index.js` and re-exported by the package root (`import { fork } from \'css-tree\'`).\n\n### 6. Test harness\n- Runner: **mocha**, not pytest.\n- Command (from `package.json` `scripts.test`):\n  ```\n  npm test\n  # == mocha lib/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter progress\n  ```\n- Single-file run:\n  ```\n  npx mocha lib/__tests/lexer.js --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter spec\n  ```\n- `lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js` installs a `__proto_pollute__` guard on `Object.prototype` (throws on non-own property reads) — relevant when adding dictionary lookups.\n- Other scripts: `test:cjs` (built `cjs/__tests`), `test:dist` (bundled `dist/__tests`), `lint` (eslint on `lib` + `scripts`), `build-and-test`.\n- Fixtures: `lib/__tests/fixture/{ast,definition-syntax,definition-syntax-match,generate-auto-emit-ws,tokenize}.js`; `forEachTest` from `lib/__tests/fixture/definition-syntax.js` drives the table-driven `valid`/`invalid` cases.\n\n### 7. Where shorthand tests should be added\nPrimary (new file, matching the existing `lexer-*.js` naming convention):\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-shorthand.js`** — new suite for shorthand expand/compress behavior.\n\nSecondary (extend existing suites):\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer.js`** — `fork()`/`createLexer()` config-level tests (e.g. shorthand definitions registered through `fork({...})`, `dump()`/recovery round-trip at `lib/__tests/lexer.js:128-170`).\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js`** — property-level matching assertions (`lexer.matchProperty(...)`, vendor-prefix/hack handling, `forEachTest` table at `:95-150`).\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-match.js`** / **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-type.js`** — if shorthand matching is exposed via `match()`/`matchType()`.\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-result.js`** — if the match result object gains shorthand-related fields.\n- **`lib/__tests/fixture/definition-syntax.js`** — if shorthand cases are added as table-driven fixtures.\n\n### 8. Caveats for the implementer\n- The task brief mentions "pytest harness" — **it does not exist in this repo**. Verify with the orchestrator whether the acceptance suite is external (hidden) or whether `npm test` is the intended gate. If a hidden Python suite exists outside the repo, it will presumably shell out to Node.\n- Shell/`python` execution is unavailable in this subagent sandbox, so no test run was performed; all findings are from static file inspection.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2088, 'prompt_tokens': 38911, 'total_tokens': 40999, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 38656}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 38656, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 255}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-fl