2026-11-27 19:46:05.395 | DEBUG    | agent.middlewares.summarization.memory_review:_invoke_memory_review:281 - memory review res is content='I have enough to report. Note: the sandbox blocked `terminal` (no OS sandbox backend for subagent scope), so all findings come from `read_file`/`search_files` only — no commands were executed.\n\n# Report: css-tree repo inspection\n\n## 1. Project shape\n- Repo root is the **css-tree** package (`package.json`: `"name": "css-tree"`, `"version": "3.2.1"`, `"type": "module"`).\n- Source lives in `lib/` (ESM), tests in `lib/__tests/`, build output in `cjs/` and `dist/`.\n- **There is no Python/pytest harness.** Zero `*.py` files exist in the repo. The test runner is **mocha** (devDependency `mocha ^9.2.2`).\n\n## 2. Test command (the "pytest equivalent")\nFrom `package.json` scripts:\n```\nnpm test\n# expands to: mocha lib/__tests --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js --reporter progress\n```\nOther relevant scripts: `npm run test:cjs` (runs `cjs/__tests`), `npm run test:dist`, `npm run lint` (`eslint lib scripts && node scripts/review-syntax-patch --lint && node scripts/update-docs --lint`), `npm run lint-and-test`.\n\nTo run a single file: `npx mocha lib/__tests/lexer.js --require lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js`.\n\n## 3. CSS lexer implementation\n| Path | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` | The `Lexer` class (511 lines) — the core implementation |\n| `lib/lexer/index.js` | Re-exports (`Lexer`, `GenericType`, etc.) |\n| `lib/lexer/create.js` | **Does not exist** — lexer creation is in `lib/syntax/create.js` |\n| `lib/lexer/match.js`, `match-graph.js`, `prepare-tokens.js`, `search.js`, `structure.js`, `trace.js`, `error.js`, `units.js`, `generic.js`, `generic-const.js` | Matching engine, token prep, fragment search, structure checks |\n| `lib/syntax/create.js` | `createSyntax(config)` — builds `syntax.lexer = new Lexer({...}, syntax)` and exposes `syntax.createLexer` / `syntax.fork` |\n| `lib/data.js`, `lib/data-patch.js` | Syntax data (mdn-data based) |\n\n### Lexer API (exact signatures, `lib/lexer/Lexer.js`)\n```js\nexport class Lexer {\n    constructor(config, syntax, structure)          // L102\n    checkStructure(ast)                             // L154\n    createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent = null)  // L173\n    addAtrule_(name, syntax)                        // L240\n    addProperty_(name, syntax)                      // L260\n    addType_(name, syntax)                          // L267\n    checkAtruleName(atruleName)                     // L275\n    checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)         // L280\n    checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName) // L299\n    checkPropertyName(propertyName)                 // L318\n    matchAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)         // L324\n    matchAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, descriptorName, value) // L339\n    matchDeclaration(node)                          // L351\n    matchProperty(propertyName, value)              // L358\n    matchType(typeName, value)                      // L372\n    match(syntax, value)                            // L381\n    findValueFragments(propertyName, value, type, name)      // L393\n    findDeclarationValueFragments(declaration, type, name)   // L396\n    findAllFragments(ast, type, name)               // L399\n    getAtrule(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)  // L412\n    getAtrulePrelude(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)    // L~420\n    getAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, name)           // L425\n    getProperty(propertyName, fallbackBasename = true)       // L430\n    getType(name)                                   // L438\n    validate()                                      // L442\n    dump(syntaxAsAst, pretty)                       // L498\n    toString()                                      // L508\n}\n```\nInternal helpers in the same file: `dumpMapSyntax`, `dumpAtruleMapSyntax`, `valueHasVar(tokens)`, `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier(syntax)`, `buildMatchResult(matched, error, iterations)`, `matchSyntax(lexer, syntax, value, useCssWideKeywords)`.\n\nInstance state: `cssWideKeywords`, `syntax`, `generic`, `units`, `atrules`, `properties`, `types`, `structure`. Descriptors are created via `createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent)` where `type ∈ {\'Property\',\'Type\',\'AtrulePrelude\',\'AtruleDescriptor\'}`; `Property` descriptors get a lazy `matchRef` getter (L217+).\n\n## 4. Existing shorthand handling\n**None.** A content search for `shorthand` / `Shorthand` across `lib/` (and `*.js`, `*.json`, `*.md`) returned **zero matches**. There is no shorthand expansion, no `shorthand` descriptor field, no `expandShorthand`-style API. Any shorthand feature must be added from scratch — the natural insertion points are:\n- `Lexer` class in `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` (new method(s) + descriptor metadata in `createDescriptor`/`addProperty_`),\n- `lib/syntax/create.js` if config plumbing is needed,\n- `lib/data.js` / `lib/data-patch.js` if shorthand definitions come from data.\n\n## 5. `fork()` custom-syntax support\n- Implementation: `lib/syntax/create.js` L31–39:\n  ```js\n  fork(extension) {\n      const base = mix({}, config);            // copy of config\n      return createSyntax(\n          typeof extension === \'function\'\n              ? extension(base)                // function form: receives base config\n              : mix(base, extension)           // object form: merged over base\n      );\n  }\n  ```\n- Config merge helper: `lib/syntax/config/mix.js`.\n- Exported from `lib/index.js` (L29: `fork` is destructured from `syntax`).\n- Usage patterns in tests: `fork({ properties: { color: \'| foo\' }, types: { ... } })` (append with `|`), and `fork(prev => ({ ...prev, ...customLexer.dump() }))` (recovery from dump) — see `lib/__tests/lexer.js` L98–122 and L160–169.\n- `fork()` is also exercised in `lib/__tests/common.js` (L56–58) and `lib/__tests/parse-extension.js`.\n\n## 6. Test files where shorthand tests should be added\nPrimary (lexer behavior):\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer.js`** — general lexer behavior, `createLexer`, `fork`, `dump`/recovery, `validate()`. Best home for a `describe(\'shorthand\', ...)` block.\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-property.js`** — `matchProperty` assertions (the closest analogue for shorthand matching).\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-type.js`**, **`lib/__tests/lexer-match.js`**, **`lib/__tests/lexer-match-result.js`** — matching semantics / result shape.\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-check-property-name.js`**, **`lib/__tests/lexer-check-structure.js`** — name/structure validation.\n- **`lib/__tests/lexer-search-fragments.js`** — fragment search (relevant if shorthand expansion affects `findValueFragments`).\n\nSupporting:\n- `lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js` (mocha require hook), `lib/__tests/common.js` (shared fixtures, `fork()` test), `lib/__tests/parse-extension.js` (fork-based syntax extension patterns).\n\n## 7. Caveats for the implementer\n- **Do not run `python -m pytest`** — it will fail (no Python tests). Use `npm test` / `npx mocha ...`.\n- `terminal` is unavailable in this subagent scope (sandbox policy), so the test suite was **not** executed here; the commands above are taken verbatim from `package.json`.\n- `lib/lexer/create.js` does not exist; don\'t create a duplicate — extend `lib/syntax/create.js` and `lib/lexer/Lexer.js`.\n- Tests import from the package root (`import { lexer, createLexer, fork } from \'css-tree\'`), resolved via `lib/__tests/helpers/setup.js`.' additional_kwargs={'refusal': None} response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2021, 'prompt_tokens': 32941, 'total_tokens': 34962, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'audio_tokens': None, 'cached_tokens': 32768}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 32768, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 173}, 'model_provider': 'deepseek', 'model_name': 'deepseek-flash', 'system_fingerprint': 'bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6', 'id': 'febba386-45e4-4dc3-ba3f-cd15d5556dae', 'finish_reason': 'sto