exer, syntax, value, useCssWideKeywords)`\n\n`class Lexer`:\n- `constructor(config, syntax, structure)` — sets `cssWideKeywords`, `syntax`, `generic`, `units`, `atrules`, `properties`, `types`, `structure`; consumes `config.{cssWideKeywords,units,types,generic,atrules,properties}`; ends with `this.cssWideKeywordsSyntax = buildMatchGraph(this.cssWideKeywords.join(\' |  \'))`.\n- `checkStructure(ast)` → `warns[] | false`\n- `createDescriptor(syntax, type, name, parent = null)` — lazy `syntax`/`match` getters; for `type === \'Property\'` defines lazy `matchRef` (uses `syntaxHasTopLevelCommaMultiplier`).\n- `addAtrule_(name, syntax)`, `addProperty_(name, syntax)`, `addType_(name, syntax)`\n- `checkPropertyName(propertyName)`, `checkAtruleName(atruleName)`, `checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)`, `checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName)`\n- `matchAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)` → `matchSyntax(this, atrule.prelude, prelude || \'\', false)`\n- `matchAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, descriptorName, value)`\n- `matchDeclaration(node)` → `this.matchProperty(node.property, node.value)`\n- `matchProperty(propertyName, value)` → rejects custom properties, `checkPropertyName`, then `matchSyntax(this, this.getProperty(propertyName), value, true)`\n- `matchType(typeName, value)`, `match(syntax, value)`\n- `findValueFragments(propertyName, value, type, name)`, `findDeclarationValueFragments(declaration, type, name)`, `findAllFragments(ast, type, name)`\n- `getAtrule(atruleName, fallbackBasename = true)`, `getAtrulePrelude(...)`, `getAtruleDescriptor(atruleName, name)`, `getProperty(propertyName, fallbackBasename = true)`, `getType(name)`\n- `validate()`, `dump(pretty, syntaxAsAst)`, `toString()`\n\n### 4. Shorthand handling\n- **No shorthand-specific code exists.** Content search for `shorthand` across the repo returned **0 matches**; there is no `lib/lexer/shorthand*` module and no shorthand branch in `matchProperty`. Shorthand expansion would be new work, most naturally hooked into `matchProperty` / `createDescriptor` in `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` (plus a new `lib/lexer/shorthand.js` if a table is needed).\n\n### 5. `fork()` custom syntax support\n- `fork` appears in 11 files: `lib/lexer/Lexer.js` (3), `lib/lexer/match.js` (3), `lib/lexer/match-graph.js` (3), `lib/lexer/match-type.js` (2), `lib/lexer/match-property.js` (3), `lib/lexer/match-atrule-prelude.js` (2), `lib/lexer/match-atrule-descriptor.js` (2), `lib/lexer/check-structure.js` (3), `lib/lexer/common.js` (13), `lib/lexer/parse-extension.js` (3), `lib/lexer/index.js` (1), `lib/lexer/create.js` (1).\n- Interpretation: `fork()` is the internal match-graph state-cloning primitive used by the backtracking matcher (`match.js` / `match-graph.js` / `common.js`), not a user-facing "custom syntax" API. Any shorthand expansion must be fork-safe (i.e. operate on the token stream / graph before matching, not mutate shared match state).\n\n### 6. Where shorthand tests should be added\n- Primary: `lib/__tests/lexer/` (Mocha suite run by `npm test`). Existing lexer test files follow the `lexer-*.js` naming seen in the file listing (`lexer-match-property.js`, `lexer-match.js`, `lexer-match-type.js`, `lexer-check-property-name.js`, `lexer-check-structure.js`, `lexer-search-fragments.js`, …). Add shorthand cases to `lib/__tests/lexer/lexer-match-property.js` (and a new `lib/__tests/lexer/lexer-shorthand.js` if a dedicated suite is preferred).\n- Fixtures: `lib/__tests/fixtures/` (syntax/`*.json` fixtures are used by the lexer tests).\n- Mirrors that must stay green: `cjs/__tests` (generated by `npm run esm-to-cjs`) and `dist/__tests` (generated by `npm run bundle`) — do not hand-edit these.\n\n### 7. Caveats for the parent agent\n- `terminal` is unusable in this subagent context: `Sandboxed execution refused: SANDBOX_POLICY=auto and no OS sandbox backend is available ... caller_scope=subagent has no operator approval path`. So I could not run `npm test` or `ls`; all findings come from `rea